+## 84. WAL-preserving snapshot rebase and writer-queue attribution — 2026-10-22
+
+The resumed M4 mission continued with a research-only change to `snapshot_rebase`: when WAL is enabled, compaction no longer synchronously flushes the pending delta at publication. It scans uncommitted WAL deletes at snapshot capture/publication, accounts for concurrent deletes in run dead-count/tombstone metadata, publishes only through `durable_wal_seq_`, and retains the later delta in WAL for normal flush/replay. WAL-disabled fallback is unchanged. Correctness coverage checks concurrent upsert/delete publication, reopen/replay, and a pre-manifest fault after tombstone output.
+
+One uniquely identified fixed-resource operation, `m4-lock-contention-microbench-20261022-131543-f71669`, returned `PASS` with zero writer/reader/durability/coherence failures and verified unit cleanup. Directional, one-run figures for `snapshot_rebase`: writer p95 16.359 ms, state-lock wait p95 15.578 ms, compaction state-lock hold 2.684 ms, pending flush 0.0029 ms; prior flush-on-publication run `122634-842053` measured 32.254/31.096/17.729/14.855 ms. Binaries and host conditions differ; this is not a controlled A/B. More importantly, the executable policy's semantic text had not yet been updated when the candidate ran: it still said publication flushes pending deltas. The raw receipt's policy hash is preserved; treat this operation as descriptive prototype evidence only, not a policy-matched or performance-eligible result. The reason is now documented, and policy JSON/Markdown plus a regression test have been updated to reflect the WAL-backed tail; the run was not rewritten or repeated. Resource/containment limits and measurement eligibility rules were not changed.
+
+The operation's workspace traversal is non-atomic with no verified lifetime peak (`performance_eligible=false`). The historical MemAvailable envelope comparison was below its threshold and explicitly unenforced in this resource-only exploratory mode; the separate 3-GiB reserve and hard containment limits remained in force. Host pressure is uncontrolled context. Complete raw evidence and limitations are in [`ANALYSIS-20261022.md`](../../research/m4-native/results/lock-contention-microbench/ANALYSIS-20261022.md), [`operation-plan.json`](../../research/m4-native/results/lock-contention-microbench/20261022/m4-lock-contention-microbench-20261022-131543-f71669/operation-plan.json), and the active [checkpoint](../../research/m4-native/results/ACTIVE-EXECUTION.md).
